AB  - Safe disposal and sustainable utilization of combustion/incineration residues derived from thermal power plant have attracted more attention from academic and industrial world. This chapter summarizes the key achievements and proposed future directions on purification technologies and sustainable recycling routes. Various thermal and nonthermal methods have been verified on heavy metals immobilization and dioxin such as compounds degradation. Howevdder, fast and low-carbon routes for one-step detoxification of hazardous ashes are still lack. Construction materials seem to be a safe and convenient destination for various ashes due to the similar mineral compositions with widely used cement, while long-term monitoring would also be required to evaluate the comprehensive environmental impacts. Moreover, seeking innovative methods to recovery valuable metals and synthesize functional materials from combustion/incineration residues are prospective to increase the economical profits, while combined technologies are usually recommended for industrial applications with the aid of life cycle assessment and cost–benefit analysis.
