AB  - Municipal solid waste incineration fly ash (MSWI FA) is one of the major by-products of municipal solid waste incineration. The recycling of MSWI FA to produce environmentally friendly cement is a promising approach. Literature has illustrate the employment of MSWI FA in the production of ordinary Portland cement (OPC) and calcium sulfoaluminate cement (CSA) clinker. Therefore, this chapter aims to consolidate the research findings in this field. This chapter will provide an overview of the mineral composition of MSWI FA, techniques for treating inorganic and organic pollutants, strategies for OPC and CSA cement clinker production, analyses of cement hydration products, performance evaluation of the MSWI FA-based products, and assessment of the life cycle of these cement clinker. This chapter focuses on the utilization of MSWI FA as an eco-cement after the calcination process, excluding its application as a supplementary cementitious material through simple mixing. Additionally, this chapter will illuminate the reaction mechanism of producing eco-cement from MSWI FA, which would foster the next-generation design of MSWI FA-derived cement.
