AB  - Concrete materials and structures have indeed exerted a transformative impact on the world and will continue in shaping the future. The extensive application of concrete in infrastructure, however, results in a considerable impact on resources, energy, and the environment. To promote their sustainable development, various forms of sustainable concrete materials and structures have been developed, involving several technical routes, such as modification of cement performance, reduction of cement/concrete consumption, development of new sustainable binders, utilization of supplementary cementitious materials, use of industrial wastes, recycle materials, and regional natural materials, adoption of advanced manufacturing/construction technology, enhancement of performance, and development of functional/smart performance. Meanwhile, for achieving net-zero emissions, some key strategies and considerations for achieving net-zero emissions have been used, such as reducing CO2 emissions from cement production, developing less intensive carbon emitters binders, carbon capture and storage technologies, use of recycled aggregates and locally sourced materials to reduce transportation-related emissions, improve the energy efficiency of concrete production processes, reduce energy consumption and emissions, optimize the use of concrete by adopting innovative technologies, for example, 3D printing technology and enhancing concrete performance for less cement use or thermal energy storage of concrete. Moreover, the sustainable development of concrete materials and structures continues to face challenges before widespread implementation, such as potential introduction of new environmental and energy-related challenges, scalable and cost-effective sustainable concrete manufacturing technologies, more potential forms, long-term performance data, and life-cycle assessment and design standard of sustainable concrete materials and structures. In conclusion, sustainable concrete materials and structures offer promise for the future, yet there is still a significant journey ahead to fully realize their potential.
