AB  - This chapter defines alkaline-activated slag cements and concrete (AASCC), focusing on emphasizing the characteristics and properties induced by ground blast furnace slags as precursors and alkaline activators. The current state of knowledge is presented regarding the behaviour of these AASCC in the fresh (rheology, setting times, etc.) and hardened states (mechanical strengths as drying shrinkage), as well as their stable behaviour and durability against different physical and chemical aggressions. Given the characteristics of these AASCC, the most appropriate applications of these materials in the construction sector are indicated. Finally, their effect on the environment, their contribution to the carbon footprint and their life cycle are assessed.
