AB  - Abstract:
This chapter describes and provides data on relevant technological, economic and environmental aspects of operating construction and demolition waste (CDW) recycling facilities which, among other output materials (e.g. wood, plastics, metals), produce average to high-quality recycled concrete aggregates. It defines and frames what is meant by recycled concrete aggregates’ quality and what it might take to achieve, at an industrial level, that same quality. Market and economic conditions are discussed, focusing on the CDW recycling facility perspective, as well as environmental consequences of its operation, in a life-cycle assessment (LCA) approach.
