AB  - Because it is fundamental to guarantee the use of recycled aggregate (RA) concrete from a structural point of view in such a way that no doubts remain concerning its safety, this chapter intends to define, apply and validate a methodology to create an equivalent functional unit (EFU) for recycled aggregate concrete. The chapter is comprised of the following parts: the definition of the declared and functional unit, where these concepts are clearly defined in order to understand the subsequent discussion; a discussion of how RA concrete performs relative to natural aggregate concrete, depending not on the aggregates’ type and content but also on the property analysed; the methodology for the definition of an EFU for RA concrete; proposal of an EFU for RA concrete; the application and validation in reinforced concrete slabs; and a survey of previous life cycle assessment studies.
