AB  - Ten comparative life cycle assessments of reinforced concrete slab life cycle were performed. Analysed slab was from a typical floor structure of residential buildings and made either of conventional [natural aggregate concrete (NAC)] or recycled aggregate concrete (RAC). The goal was to investigate the influence of recycled concrete aggregate (RCA) quality, the slab’s durability, life cycle inventory modelling approach and CO2 uptake on the assessment results. All comparisons were based on the functional unit which provided full functional equivalence between slab alternatives. In order to calculate the amount of reference flows, both NAC and RAC slabs were designed according to Eurocodes. Results showed that the influence of the modelling approach on impact indicators and influence of CO2 uptake on the global warming potential was more significant (up to 25%) than the influence of the RCA quality and concrete durability for exposure classes (up to 8%).
