AB  - Energy consumption and greenhouse gas release in mining and refining of chemically bonded phosphate ceramic (CBPC) components, and production of CBPC cements and coatings are calculated using the US Environmental Protection Agency’s Core Module Guidelines recommended for ordinary Portland cement. The results show that the energy consumed in producing CBPC cements is 45% and greenhouse gas release is only 26% of ordinary Portland cement. Similarly the greenhouse gas release in the case of CBPC coatings is only a fraction of similar coatings products. Other environmental factors, such as production of volatile organic compounds and hazardous air products, are simply absent in the case of CBPC products, and acidification and eutrophication are negligible. Detailed life-cycle assessment is needed but can only be done once the CBPC products are on the market and full life-cycle footprints are known.
