AB  - Concrete pavements are widely used to carry heavy load and provide long-lasting solutions in highways, airports, and bridge decks. This chapter reviews the current state-of-practice in lifecycle cost analysis (LCCA) and lifecycle assessment (LCA) of concrete pavement repairs. Most studies focused on pavement rehabilitation alternatives, especially different overlay types, with assumption of relatively small contribution from routine maintenance of concrete pavement. Compared to the agency cost invested in the construction stage and the environmental burden brought by raw material and manufacturing, the impact of work zones on the cost of traveling public and the emission generated in the usage stage of pavement cannot be neglected. The integration of economic analysis and environmental assessment is critical to develop eco-efficient concrete pavement repair solutions for multiple-objective decision making. Future research recommendations are discussed for the purpose of improving accuracy of LCCA and LCA for the overall sustainability.
