AB  - This chapter reports on the sustainability of concrete and provides an assessment on the carbon footprint of concrete from the life-cycle aspect and environmental impact perspectives, with a special focus on cement and cement replacement materials used in construction. The life-cycle assessment of concrete includes information on the production of raw materials for concrete, the manufacturing of concrete, the use of supplementary materials such as fly ash and ground-granulated, blast-furnace slag, chemical admixtures, and on the recycling of concrete. Lowering the environmental impact of concrete by using partial replacement of cement, improving cement production, the development of alternative binders, recycling waste byproducts, and the enhancement of durability is presented. This chapter includes some information on modern concrete, such as self-compacting and geopolymer concrete, and future trends in concrete.
