AB  - A life cycle analysis of selected sustainable geopolymer concrete mixtures is presented with a focus on the thermal energy and associated CO2 emissions compared to conventional ordinary Portland cement (OPC) concrete, which is a major contributor to global CO2 emissions. Geopolymer concrete, a more sustainable alternative to OPC, shows lower thermal energy and CO2 emissions across all concrete classifications. In three of the four classes of concrete, two geopolymer mixtures are compared—one with sodium silicate as the binder and another using fly ash. Mixtures using fly ash as a binder show the lowest thermal energy consumption and CO2 emissions. Sodium hydroxide is a significant contributor to the energy and CO2 emission of geopolymer mixtures and researchers continue to look for alternatives.
