AB  - This chapter addresses the topic of residues from thermochemical processes for treating urban organic municipal solid waste (OMSW), more specifically incinerated municipal solid waste (MSWI) ash, by studying how to reintroduce this ash into the production chain, by considering its use as a civil construction material. Ash can be categorized as either fly ash or bottom ash, and both have different physical and chemical properties, which will be presented in this chapter, followed by detailing the properties of fresh and hardened concrete, as well as the durability characteristics. The codes and standards for these materials and processes are shown here, along with MSWI leaching analysis studies for mortars prepared with MSWI. Cost analysis was also conducted along with a life cycle analysis. This chapter will also present the results for the studies conducted for MSWI and potential benefits and / or limitations of using this material in civil construction.
