AB  - In this chapter, we introduce the methodology for evaluating life cycle in research on cement-based materials. First, we explain the necessity of managing the carbon emissions from the manufacture of construction materials, in particular cement production. Then, we examine the environmental impacts at different stages of the life cycle of cement production. This chapter points out the magnitude of consumption of fossil fuels and nonrenewable energy during manufacturing and highlights the environmental impacts of significant global warming, toxicity to human health, and scarcity of natural resources as a result of this manufacturing. The information presented in this chapter may be used to assess environmental impacts of cement-based material manufacturing and to enrich the methods for sustainable development and environmental protection, such as by supporting the use of supplementary cementitious material wastes.
