AB  - Cementitious SSC’s are long-lived, and their life cycle starts outside the nuclear industry and extends during the operational, closure, and postclosure phases of the nuclear facility. This chapter introduces the life cycle of the cementitious systems in active and passive safety environments by introducing to preoperational, operational, and postoperational phases. In this respect, life cycle management will be introduced and the preoperational phases of different cement-based materials will be summarized. The design phase will be highlighted with a special reference to the design phase for radioactive waste disposal facility. The international guideline and national regulations and codes and standards used to design the nuclear reactor containment will be briefed. The international atomic energy agency guidelines for the design of spent fuel storage will be presented. Finally, operational and postoperational phases will be briefly introduced.
