AB  - The environmental impacts arising from the cement and concrete industry are diverse and need to be assessed and discussed. The amount of CO2 and other greenhouse gases generated in the manufacture of these materials can be drastically minimized if the concrete industry's production techniques are more efficient. However, it is not enough to assess the environmental impacts of the production process. Instead, a holistic assessment is necessary, considering the entire concrete life cycle. From this growing awareness, the Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) methodology has been widely used to evaluate the environmental impacts of all the processes associated with concrete. This work intends to discuss the LCA application to evaluate structural and non-structural concrete, both widely used in the construction sector worldwide and responsible for a large number of environmental impacts. The study is based on international technical standards, the content of which is also discussed and evaluated in this work. Therefore, it is expected to assist in a better understanding of the environmental impacts of structural and non-structural concrete and their respective management.
