AB  - To achieve sustainability in construction, selection of material plays an important role. As construction industry largely depend on resources and hence material selected should follow all the principles of sustainability. A Comprehensive review of methods for selecting construction material is carried out and found that very few studies are available for deciding the alternatives for coarse aggregates. In the present study for a framework along with case study for selecting best sustainable material among given alternatives has been carried out. Performance of selected material is studied through its three phases of life cycle i.e. Pre-Construction phase, Construction phase and Post-Construction phase, considering all sustainable criteria and indicators. In the present study, sustainable factors such as Environmental, Economic, Social and Technological are examined for various coarse aggregate materials through the discussion and questionnaire from stakeholders and experts, the output in the form of sustainable score is evaluated using a Multi criteria decision making technique, Analytical Hierarchy Process (AHP) to determine the best material among the available alternatives for the three ingredients of concrete. The alternative with highest sustainable score is assigned as best sustainable material among given alternatives. The findings of the study that among five alternative of coarse aggregate (crushed gravel, recycled gravel, bloated clay, granulated blast slag, sintered flyash), crushed gravel shows highest score of 1.03. The outcome of this study helps design engineers in selecting the best sustainable alternative in the mix design.
