AB  - Construction sector is a very important sector in Europe, especially in southern countries like Spain, Italy, Greece where there is a strong infrastructure development because they are still lagging behind Northern countries. Approximately 34.7% of total waste production in Europe is related to buildings construction and demolition. European directive 2008/98/EC imposes that by 2020, 70% in mass of demolition waste will have to be recycled. The objective set by the legislation is excellent from the point of view of the circular economy, not producing wastes; but is it also good from an environmental point of view? Life Cycle Assessment tries to answer these questions by indicating whether it is an ecological route or not. Thus, in the present work the impact related to the building construction using reinforcing concrete is analyzed using two types of concrete. The first is made with recycled aggregates and the other one with natural aggregates. To complete the analysis, the impact of a building construction employing geopolymer concrete mixtures is also assessed.
