AB  - The use of eco-efficient pavement materials is crucial for addressing environmental concerns, minimizing waste generation, conserving energy, and optimizing resource utilization in pavement construction. By incorporating sustainable practices and materials such as recycled aggregates and waste materials, we can reduce environmental impact and promote a more sustainable and resource-efficient approach to building and maintaining pavements. This book chapter offers a comprehensive and contemporary review of eco-efficient pavement materials. It presents the latest advancements and knowledge in sustainable practices and materials used in pavement construction. The chapter covers a range of topics, including the utilization of scrap plastics in asphalt binders, the analysis of microstructure and performance characteristics of cold recycled asphalt mixtures, the assessment of life cycle studies on asphalt pavement recycling, and the incorporation of recycled concrete aggregates in pavement base/subbase courses. The chapter serves as an up-to-date resource for researchers, practitioners, and policymakers interested in understanding and implementing eco-efficient approaches in pavement construction.
