AB  - Breakthroughs in sustainable approaches to pavement have been a focus of recent research efforts. This chapter explores the cutting-edge field of eco-efficient pavement construction materials as well as examines the sustainable options that have the potential to reshape the approach to infrastructure development. The objective is to present a comprehensive synthesis of the revolutionary breakthroughs in paving materials. Besides, different methodological approaches, such as the examination of recently published peer-reviewed research publications, have been utilized to provide a robust, multidimensional perspective. Therefore this chapter includes a review that encompasses current developments in the field of pavement engineering involving the usage of waste products, self-healing concrete, and nanotechnology with their practical uses. These advancements, while simultaneously preserving natural resources, help enhance energy efficiency and mitigate the release of greenhouse gases. In addition, the chapter offers valuable perspectives on the life cycle analysis of these materials, emphasizing their enduring economic and environmental sustainability. This investigation seeks to provide a revolutionary review of sustainable practices in the manufacture of concrete, with the ultimate goal of promoting a new age of environmentally efficient pavement construction approaches. This chapter suggests that the sustainability analysis of chosen recycled materials is still in its early stages and needs more investigation. Therefore further research is required to acquire a better understanding of these implications in order for policymakers to be able to make decisions that are better informed.
