AB  - Sustainable development considers the magnitude of the impact of the construction industry on the environment and helps to restore the ecological balance. In other words, increasing the efficiency of resources and materials throughout the life cycle of a structure is aided by sustainable development in construction. Concrete is the most important material utilized for the development of a country and cement is also one of the most important elements in concrete. One of the goals is to replace cement with POFA as partial replacement and it has properties similar to cement that react as binder and also can help to improve strength. Three types of the specimen have been analyses. For example, the control (OPC), 10% POFA with 2% PET (10P2P) and 10% POFA with 4% PET (10P4P) Not only use POFA as an innovative technique in this study, but also investigated the possibility of treating PET with 8 mol sulphuric acid as an additive. After the casting process, the flow table test was conducted for fresh concrete in order to determine the concrete consistency. A rebound hammer test was performed to check the concrete quality for the non-destructive test of hardened concrete, and a compression test was performed to analyse the concrete strength for the destructive test. As a result, the consistency of concrete with POFA and PET was higher than OPC concrete, while for the compression test, the strength of OPC concrete was higher than concrete that contained POFA and PET. © 2022 American Institute of Physics Inc.. All rights reserved.
