AB  - The primary objective of this paper is to develop the product data
models, in which systematic information is defined for accumulating,
exchanging, and sharing in the maintenance of concrete highway bridges.
The information requirement and existing issues and solutions were
analyzed based on the life cycle and the standardization for sharing.
The member data models and business data models that defined design and
construction information and accumulated results information were
developed. The maintenance business process in which project
participants utilize the product data model was described as utilization
scenario. The utilization frameworks which define information flow were
developed.
