AB  - This paper validates Dewar's particle packing modelling (PPM) theory for
implementing both fine and coarse recycled concrete aggregates (RCAs)
from using aggregates with multi-size classes (0/1, 0/4, 2/8, 0/8, 8/20,
0/20). The voids ratios of aggregate mixtures were evaluated
experimentally and compared with the predictions. The model shows high
predicting accuracy for implementing coarse RCA. A size ratio adjustment
factor might be necessary to calibrate the model for implementing fine
RCA and all in fractions (0/8, 0/20). A practical method for evaluating
this factor is proposed. The powder within the investigated aggregates
has limited impact on the estimation of the voids ratio of aggregate
mixtures. However, the powder fraction shall have an effect on the final
mix design as well as on the fresh and hardened concrete properties.
