AB  - In marine environment, integral hydrophobic cement mortar (IHCM) can provide effective protection for steel bars. But, the significant decrease in strength and the environmental impacts of IHCM cannot be ignored. Stearic acid emulsion (SAE), siloxane emulsion (SE) and silica fume (SF) were applied to prepare IHCM. Mechanical strength, water absorption, wettability, corrosion resistance and environmental impacts of IHCM were studied. The results indicated the compressive strength of IHCM with SAE and SE reached 38.7–42.6 MPa and 49.5–58.0 MPa at 28 days, respectively, and then increased to 46.4–61.8 MPa and 71.2–82.5 MPa at 180 days. The water absorption of IHCM was much lower than normal cement mortar. For IHCM with SAE and SE, the water contact angle reached 147.8°–150.5° and 146.0°–154.1°, respectively. Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy, X-ray diffraction and scanning electron microscope results proved the combined effect of hydrophobic agent and SF endowed IHCM with good hydrophobicity and high strength. According to the sulfuric acid resistance test and electrochemical test, IHCM showed better corrosion resistance than normal cement mortar, and could protect steel bars from corrosion. Besides, the global warming potential of IHCM with SAE and SE decreased by 15.13% and 15.73% compared with normal cement mortar through life cycle assessment, respectively.
