AB  - To study the life-cycle seismic reliability analysis (SRA) of
cable-stayed bridges (CSBs) taking into account chloride-induced
corrosion and degradation of components, an actual railway CSB with
uncertainties in structural geometry and material corrosion coefficients
was employed in this investigation, and time-dependent models of CSB
components at different service times were studied. Based on the
OpenSees batch program, we adapted a mass numerical computation to
obtain time-dependent non-linear seismic response and probability
density function (PDF) of response via the multiplier
dimensional-reduction method (MDRM) and the maximum entropy method with
fractional moments (FM-MEM). Next, the time-dependent failure
possibility of every component and the association coefficient between
the failure modes of different parts were acquired. In the end, the
product of the conditional marginal (PCM) approach was employed to
obtain the life-cycle failure possibility of the CSB system. The results
showed that the system failure possibility of the CSB in a corrosive
environment increases significantly with increasing servicing time.
