AB  - In this study, the earthquakes effect on integral bridges is examined,
through computer simulation of an integral abutment bridge. The study is
made based on Eurocode 8 recommendations. For the analysis, a
symmetrical medium length integral bridge obtained from an existing
structure is used. Both static and dynamic relative displacement studies
are carried out to develop insight as to the significance or dominance
of either dynamic or relative displacement effects. The final aim of
this study is to conduct prediction of dynamic response of the bridge
after applying the earthquake vertically and horizontally. The time
histories were used to carry full integration time history analyses in
to simulate the dynamic response of the bridge. The results show that
relative displacements play an important role in overall structural
response of the integral bridge, compared to the pure dynamic response.
