AB  - This paper proposes a modified process analysis method that combines
with the input-output method for carbon emissions assessment in slurry
shield tunnel construction. The method was applied to analyze the carbon
emissions generated during the construction procedures of a slurry
shield tunnel. The results indicate that the carbon emissions from
building materials account for the majority of the total emissions,
while those from the shield machine and construction procedure are
relatively small. In addition, BP and CNN-LSTM neural network models
were established to validate the accuracy of the calculation results
with model error of 0.1031. Finally, recommendations for reducing carbon
emissions in the construction course of slurry shield tunnels are
provided.
