AB  - At present, all kinds of sports are popularized more and more deeply all
over the world, and the accompanying sports waste has caused great
pressure on the natural environment, but the society pays far less
attention to the reuse of sports waste. Based on this, waste badminton
shuttlecock (WBS) with an annual consumption of over 300 million in
China was selected for asphalt modification. Combined with penetration,
softening point, temperature scanning, multiple stress creep recovery,
linear amplitude sweep test, bending-beam rheometer test and infrared
spectrum test, its performance and mechanism were tested. The results
showed that WBS can significantly improve the high-temperature
performance of asphalt and improve its low-temperature performance to a
certain extent, but when the content is too high, it is unfavorable to
its fatigue performance, and it is recommended that the content should
be within 1%. The infrared spectrum test results showed that the
modification process is physical miscible modification. This study can
provide inspiration and thinking for the application of sports waste in
road materials, and further benefit analysis can be carried out in the
future combined with life cycle cost calculation.
