AB  - A major challenge for society is to reduce the effects of greenhouse
gases (GHG), one of the causes of climate change, generated by the
increase of waste released into the environment. This study sought to
evaluate the results obtained from GHG emissions due to waste treatment
techniques such as disposal in landfill, incineration and recycling.
Different waste management scenarios were created. The methodology was
used to help define the best solution for municipal solid waste (MSW)
and Construction and Demolition Waste (CDW), management planning in the
city of S & atilde;o Jose dos Campos, in the state of S & atilde;o
Paulo, Brazil. The study found that landfill disposal, the most applied
technique in Brazil, has many disadvantages. It was concluded that the
incineration of MSW showed more favorable results in relation to CO2
emissions and energy consumption. The benefits of incinerating MSW and
recycling CDW for use as aggregates in concrete have been demonstrated.
