AB  - This paper presents the results of the sensitivity analysis performed
for the sustainability assessment model of the Spanish Code on
Structural Concrete, EHE-08. It also portrays the results of a
life-cycle analysis (LCA) related to energy consumption and CO2
emissions. Comparisons are made between those findings, for suggesting
improvements to the model. The main conclusion is that some weights and
value functions employed in the EHE-08 are not consistent with the LCA.
The new versions of the Spanish Code should include other weights and
value functions to get closer to the LCA results.
