AB  - The in-depth research on efficient processes and alternative
constituents for mortars production has a lack on the quantification of
their environmental impacts. This work presents a critical review of
life cycle assessment (LCA) studies performed in the construction
sector, namely related to mortars. The gaps and barriers of these
methods and final results are discussed through an overview of the main
achievements on mortars' environmental life cycle studies in Europe.
Despite the future trends, LCA studies are more focused on
cement-mortars and few researches on air lime, gypsum or earth mortar
binders are reported in the literature.
