AB  - The Dutch Ministry of Infrastructure and the Environment is concerned
with the safety of existing infrastructure and assessment thereof, which
can be done with nonlinear finite element analysis. The 2017 updated
version of the Dutch NLFEA Guidelines can be used for reinforced and
prestressed beams and slabs. The purpose of the guidelines is twofold:
1) advice analysists on NLFEA of concrete structures, and 2) explain
choices and model uncertainty. This paper introduces the latest version
of the guideline, and shows the application for a reinforced concrete
slab on top of a concrete beam grid. An overheight vehicle caused damage
to the concrete cover and the reinforcement of the beams. The analysis
shows the results of modeling the bridge without and with damage. The
outcome of the assessment is that the structure fulfils the code
requirements. This case study shows that the Dutch NLFEA Guidelines can
be used for the assessment of damaged concrete bridges.
