AB  - A multi-criteria decision-making system based on the MIVES method is
presented as a model for assessing the global sustainability index
scores of existing wind-turbine support systems. This model is
specifically designed to discriminate between tower systems in order to
minimize the subjectivity of the decision and, thus, facilitate the task
of deciding which system is best for a given set of boundary conditions
(e. g., height, turbine power, soil conditions) and economic, social and
environmental requirements. The model's versatility is proven by
assessing the sustainability index of an innovative new precast concrete
tower alternative also described in this paper. As a result of this
analysis, some points of improvement in the new system have been
detected.
