AB  - Suez-ResourceCo in Adelaide is a Construction & Demolition and
Commercial & Industrial waste processing facility that produces
alternative fuel for the local cement kiln operation. In recent years,
Australia has seen an increase in energy cost and the state of South
Australia has experienced a significant rise: approximately 29%
increase in wholesale electricity price (2015/16 to 2016/17). Although
the facility has been monitoring energy consumption at the gate level,
the highly variable profile and many assets in operation have motivated
the facility to conduct an energy flow analysis. The study identifies
key assets for sub-metering to understand their energy profile and
validate overall energy flow of the facility. The result outlines how
the design paradigm of the waste industry has led to vastly over-sized
plant leading to low efficiencies and power factors. Hence, potential
energy and GHG saving is quantified through proposed efficiency gains.
